<title>USA: Openness key to effective policy -- Bank of Canada.</title>
<headline>Openness key to effective policy -- Bank of Canada.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Bank openness about the monetary policy process is an important element of an effective monetary policy, Bank of Canada Deputy Governor Charles Freedman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Openness has made the monetary policy process clearly, absolutely, more effective. It functions better,&quot; Freedman told Reuters at a Bank Administration Institute conference on the U.S. payments system.</p>
<p>Freedman also said central banks are looking more than ever at market behavior and expectations as sources of information in the policy-making process.</p>
</text>
